<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - LastTheWord</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0b0d12;
            --card-bg: #141721;
            --text-main: #e2e8f0;
            --text-muted: #94a3b8;
            --accent-color: #38bdf8;
            --border-color: #1e293b;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: var(--bg-color);
            color: var(--text-main);
            line-height: 1.6;
            padding: 40px 20px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            width: 100%;
            background-color: var(--card-bg);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 40px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
        }

        header {
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
            padding-bottom: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 2rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
            color: #ffffff;
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .last-updated {
            font-size: 0.875rem;
            color: var(--text-muted);
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: #ffffff;
            margin-top: 28px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-color);
            padding-left: 10px;
        }

        p {
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            color: var(--text-main);
        }

        ul {
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            padding-left: 20px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        a {
            color: var(--accent-color);
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .contact-box {
            background-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.05);
            border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.2);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .contact-box p {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .contact-box p:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            body {
                padding: 16px 8px;
            }
            .container {
                padding: 24px 16px;
            }
            h1 {
                font-size: 1.5rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
    <header>
        <h1>Privacy Policy for LastTheWord</h1>
        <p class="last-updated">Last updated: September 9, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p>This Privacy Policy applies to the <strong>LastTheWord</strong> mobile application (the "Application"), created by <strong>Rıdvan Topal</strong> ("we," "us," or "our").</p>

    <p>We built LastTheWord with privacy and performance in mind. Core gameplay relies on a fully offline dictionary, meaning your word lookups, typing inputs, and game progress are processed locally on your device and are never transmitted to our servers.</p>

    <h2>1. Local Data Processing</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Offline Dictionary & Gameplay:</strong> All word validation, scoring, turn logic, and dictionary lookups occur entirely on your device. We do not transmit, log, or collect the words you type.</li>
        <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> Your game settings, high scores, and gameplay statistics are saved locally on your device using standard iOS system storage.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Third-Party Services & Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
    <p>To support the Application, we integrate <strong>Google AdMob</strong> to display advertisements. While core gameplay runs completely offline, Google AdMob requires a network connection to serve ads and may collect device diagnostics and ad-related data.</p>

    <p>Depending on your choices regarding Apple's <strong>App Tracking Transparency (ATT)</strong> prompt, data collected by Google AdMob may include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> Device Identifier for Advertisers (IDFA, if permitted), Identifier for Vendors (IDFV), or other advertising IDs.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> Interactions with ads shown within LastTheWord (such as ad impressions and taps).</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostics:</strong> Technical performance metrics, load times, and crash reports related to ad delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Location Data:</strong> Approximate location derived from your device's IP address.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For more details on how Google handles collected data, please visit <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Advertising Terms & Privacy</a>.</p>

    <h2>3. App Tracking Transparency (ATT) & Choice</h2>
    <p>When you launch LastTheWord, you will see Apple's <strong>App Tracking Transparency (ATT)</strong> permission prompt asking if you allow LastTheWord to track your activity across other companies' apps and websites.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>If you select "Allow":</strong> Google AdMob uses your device IDFA to show personalized advertisements tailored to your interests.</li>
        <li><strong>If you select "Ask App Not to Track" (or refuse):</strong> We do not access your IDFA. You will still see ads, but they will be contextual/non-personalized rather than based on your browsing behavior.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can update or revoke your choice at any time in your iOS settings under <strong>Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Tracking</strong>.</p>

    <h2>4. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>LastTheWord does not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13 (or 16 in certain jurisdictions). If you are a parent or guardian and believe third-party ad services have collected information from your child without consent, please contact us immediately so we can assist.</p>

    <h2>5. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date.</p>

    <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions or feedback regarding this Privacy Policy, please reach out:</p>

    <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:rdvn.tpl@gmail.com">rdvn.tpl@gmail.com</a></p>
        <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://rdvntpl.github.io/lasttheword/">https://rdvntpl.github.io/lasttheword/</a></p>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
